  "details": "\"Focus Search on Selected Node\" feature is very very useful.\nBut I'm afraid that new user might be confused and frustrated. I think frustrated user-experience is very bad than inconvenience.\nI guess the reason is there's no visual information that suggests the search window content is related to node selection.\nTwo screen shots are samples that new user will see. (After node creation, the inserted node is selected. So I guess this is very common use case.) Two search window is too much similar. so that, new user might feel like \"Left arrow disappears. why?\", \"I can't select the node what I want to add\", \"It must be a bug\"...\nI don't have certain (or concrete) idea yet. But border appearance of the window and/or help information (popup tool tip?) might change the situation. Currently (VRCSDK-UDON-2020.06.04.14.15_Closed_Community_Test) SearchWindow is implemented in Unity side. So I also understand changing appearance isn't so light task to implement.\nSo I propose alternative solution for now:\n1. Change default setting to off (do not use this feature)\n2. Add more beginner friendly information (or a link to such note) on WelcomeView\nCurrently default setting is on. Setting toggle button has tooltip text, but it too short.",
